      "writtenOn": "2018-07-17T16:43:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So we are now changing the behavior that PD task waking alone is not sufficient to exit DRP_AUTO_TOGGLE state. Presumably, this section only needs to run when there is a CC state change, but I don\u0027t know if that\u0027s *always* the case.\n\nfor example, if there is an adapter connected but the port is not allowed to be a SRC (AP !\u003d S0), then we want to got into low power mode. When the chipset power state changes, then the PD task will wake and if CC \u003d\u003d Rd, then the PD state should go SRC_DISCONNECTED, but there won\u0027t be a CC state change. Since PD_FLAGS_LPM_REQUESTED won\u0027t remain high, this specific case should still work.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3574,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 3574,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "3c5a0729b01e4429991a2a10b7aed03e315f0638",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d1d151b1_85de7ebc",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 3574,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-07-17T19:32:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I searched for all of the task_wake(PD_PORT_TO_TASK_ID(port)) calls, and the only call that could be in the AUTO_TOGGLE state is the in usb_charger [0] and similar [1] tpcp_alert.\n\nThey both have to deal with Vbus changing. Vbus would have to be off for us to be in auto toggle so vbus would theoretically be turning on. If Vbus were turning on, then we would have gotten a CC, Reset, or some other type of event as well pulling us out of auto_toggle.\n\nDoes that sounds right to you? I couldn\u0027t think of any other case where the condition on line 3573 broke down, but if you can let me know.\n\n\n[0] https://chromium.git.corp.google.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/987ad5eaed2201c41820aa7f81333e1733a124a0/common/usb_charger.c#81\n[1] https://chromium.git.corp.google.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/987ad5eaed2201c41820aa7f81333e1733a124a0/driver/tcpm/tcpci.c#345",
      "parentUuid": "a886954b_558f89f6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3574,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 3574,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "3c5a0729b01e4429991a2a10b7aed03e315f0638",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
